# Who goes first at a roundabout?
subtitle: "At a roundabout, whoever is entering gives way to traffic already on the ring, so nobody needs lights."
tags: ["traffic","roundabouts","driving","rules","road safety"]
teaches: ["concepts/roundabout-priority"]
thumb: "band \"Who goes first?\" note \"one simple rule\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a warm, clear teacher, quietly enjoying the idea"}

## Who goes first at a roundabout?
setting:
    ground: grass
    props:
      - {icon: deciduous tree, place: beside road_ew, repeat: 2}
      - {icon: house with garden, place: top right}
      - {icon: evergreen tree, place: beside road_s}

    polygon road_ew #a8a49a points [[20,357],[980,357],[980,473],[20,473]] style.fill #d6d2c8 style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.8 style.roughness 0 style.stroke_width 0.5 hidden true
    polygon road_s #a8a49a points [[442,130],[558,130],[558,357],[442,357]] style.fill #d6d2c8 style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.8 style.roughness 0 style.stroke_width 0.5 hidden true
    polygon road_n #a8a49a points [[442,473],[558,473],[558,645],[442,645]] style.fill #d6d2c8 style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.8 style.roughness 0 style.stroke_width 0.5 hidden true
    shape ring_fill #a8a49a shape circle x 500 y 415 radius 158 style.fill #d6d2c8 style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.8 style.roughness 0 style.stroke_width 0.5 hidden true
    shape island #7aa865 shape circle x 500 y 415 radius 75 style.fill #a9cf98 style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.8 style.roughness 0 hidden true
    path ring_out closed #3d3833 points [[658,415],[657,436],[653,456],[646,475],[637,494],[625,511],[612,527],[596,540],[579,552],[560,561],[541,568],[521,572],[500,573],[479,572],[459,568],[440,561],[421,552],[404,540],[388,527],[375,511],[363,494],[354,475],[347,456],[343,436],[342,415],[343,394],[347,374],[354,355],[363,336],[375,319],[388,303],[404,290],[421,278],[440,269],[459,262],[479,258],[500,257],[521,258],[541,262],[560,269],[579,278],[596,290],[612,303],[625,319],[637,336],[646,355],[653,374],[657,394]] hidden true
    path ring_in closed #3d3833 points [[575,415],[574,425],[572,434],[569,444],[565,453],[560,461],[553,468],[546,475],[538,480],[529,484],[519,487],[510,489],[500,490],[490,489],[481,487],[471,484],[463,480],[454,475],[447,468],[440,461],[435,453],[431,444],[428,434],[426,425],[425,415],[426,405],[428,396],[431,386],[435,378],[440,369],[447,362],[454,355],[462,350],[471,346],[481,343],[490,341],[500,340],[510,341],[519,343],[529,346],[538,350],[546,355],[553,362],[560,369],[565,377],[569,386],[572,396],[574,405]] hidden true
    path rd_s #3d3833 points [[442,130],[442,268]] hidden true
    path rd_s2 #3d3833 points [[558,130],[558,268]] hidden true
    path rd_n #3d3833 points [[442,562],[442,645]] hidden true
    path rd_n2 #3d3833 points [[558,562],[558,645]] hidden true
    path rd_w #3d3833 points [[20,357],[353,357]] hidden true
    path rd_w2 #3d3833 points [[20,473],[353,473]] hidden true
    path rd_e #3d3833 points [[647,357],[980,357]] hidden true
    path rd_e2 #3d3833 points [[647,473],[980,473]] hidden true
    path yield dashed thick #b5482e points [[504,254],[556,254]] hidden true
    arrow dir dashed #8a847d from.x 386 from.y 384 to.x 469 to.y 301 hidden true
    icon carA size 64 x 530 y 213 or ["red car"] flip true icon_look picture of automobile hidden true
    icon carB size 64 x 412 y 336 or ["blue car"] flip true icon_look picture of "sport utility vehicle" hidden true
    text l_A "arriving" #b5482e x 340 y 213 font_size 22 hidden true
    text l_B "on the ring" #2f6b8f x 262 y 306 font_size 22 hidden true
    text l_give "give way" #b5482e x 633 y 254 hidden true

Who goes first at a roundabout? Here traffic drives on the right.
    draw road_ew road_s road_n ring_fill island ring_out ring_in rd_s rd_s2 rd_n rd_n2 rd_w rd_w2 rd_e rd_e2

So cars on the ring circle anticlockwise, the way this arrow points.
    draw dir

A red car arrives from the south and wants to go in.
    draw carA l_A

But a blue car is already on the ring, coming round from its left.
    draw carB l_B

The rule: whoever is entering gives way to traffic already on the roundabout.
    draw yield l_give

So the red car waits at the dashed line while the blue one passes in front of it.
    move carB by [181,6] duration 1.6

(@erase l_A l_B@) Now the ring is (@move carA by [-34,86] duration 1.4@) clear to its left, and it may go in.

Everyone gives way in the same direction, so traffic keeps moving without lights, and cars never meet head on.
    text l_end "no lights needed" #4f7a3a x 270 y 600

    quiz "You are about to enter, and a car on the ring is coming from your left. Who goes first?"
        right: The car on the ring: whoever is entering gives way.
        * You, because you reached the line first
        + The car already on the ring

One rule, the same for everyone: give way to the ring.
    highlight yield
---
